It is known that   $p_k/q_k \to {\alpha}$ as $k\to \infty,$ and moreover the convergents of ${\alpha}$ satisfy the inequalities 
	\begin{equation} \label{rate}
		\frac{1}{2q_k q_{k+1}} < \left| {\alpha} - \frac{p_k}{q_k}\right| < \frac{1}{q_k q_{k+1}} \qquad (k\geqslant 1), 
	\end{equation}
	see  for example  \cite[Chapter 7.5]{NZM1991}.

From the relations \eqref{recursive}, it follows that
